1. Open Wireshark.
2. Select active Wi-Fi interface.
3. Double-click to start capture.
4. Open browser and visit any website.
5. Browse for 20–30 seconds.
6. Return to Wireshark.
7. Click Stop.

FILTERS:
dns - DNS packets
tcp - TCP packets
udp - UDP packets
tls - Encrypted TLS traffic
http - HTTP packets

8. Type dns in filter bar > Enter.
9. Select a packet.
10. Expand Domain Name System.
11. Note query name and response.
12. Type tcp > Enter.
13. Select a packet.
14. Expand Transmission Control Protocol.
15. Note source port, destination port and flags.

GRAPHS:
16. Click Statistics > Protocol Hierarchy.
17. Observe protocols.
18. Click Statistics > I/O Graphs.
19. Observe packet traffic.

OUTPUT:
- Source and destination IP
- Protocol
- Source and destination port
- Packet length
- DNS information
